.fz/models/perfectgas.json<pre><code>{
  "id": "perfectgas",
  "delim": "{}",
  "output": {"pressure": "python://grep(r'pressure = (\\S+)', 'output.txt')"}
}
</code></pre> <p>All fields: Model Definition. The file name is the alias; <code>id</code> must be set for calculator aliases to match the model.</p>

.fz/calculators/cluster.json<pre><code>{
  "uri": "ssh://user@hpc.example.edu",
  "models": {"perfectgas": "bash /home/user/codes/perfectgas/run.sh"},
  "code_id": "perfectgas@2.1"
}
</code></pre> <p>Keys: <code>uri</code>, <code>models</code> (model <code>id</code> → command), <code>code_id</code>, <code>version_cmd</code>. See Calculators. When <code>calculators</code> is omitted, every alias supporting the model's <code>id</code> is used.</p>
